0x5558448fd827ea876177c2beefc7415d539d0f5c6281745f5def259fa9002b6f  ALLOWLIST.md

keccak256 of ALLOWLIST.md's bytes, 14479 of them. Reproduce it with:

    cast keccak "0x$(xxd -p < ALLOWLIST.md | tr -d '\n')"

This value is what goes on chain, in a zero-value transaction from the deployer
before UnderwaterWaitlist is deployed — see the Publication section of the document
itself. It lives here rather than inside ALLOWLIST.md because a file cannot state
its own hash.

Amending the criteria before registration opens means: edit the document, recompute
this value, publish a new transaction, and re-pin CRITERIA_URL in web/lib/links.ts
to the commit carrying the new bytes. After registration opens the document is
final.

PUBLISHED 2026-09-04 on Robinhood Chain (4663), transaction

    0xb8dce2f26605a10de8b75c52f199d8574f879864abca2d6c168bf87125b43699

sent from the deployer 0xd41523Baff52CdEf22a513249AB7e28243527050 to itself,
zero value, carrying these 32 bytes as its entire calldata, in block 54607941 at
2026-09-04 22:06:15 UTC. Read it back off chain with:

    cast tx 0xb8dce2f26605a10de8b75c52f199d8574f879864abca2d6c168bf87125b43699 input --rpc-url robinhood

Two limits on what that transaction proves. Both belong in the announcement
rather than being quietly dropped:

  - It is NOT below S. The Publication section asks for a hash block lower than
    the waitlist's own deploy block, and the flexible waitlist
    0xD51bBB321fA47798FCb6bA59491aC499B276d726 deployed at 54204284, roughly ten
    hours earlier. That clause cannot be honoured for any contract that is
    already live, and it is not honoured here.
  - It IS below every registration. count() was still 0 in block 54607941, and
    the window does not close until 1789163160 (2026-09-11 21:46:00 UTC), so the
    criteria were fixed and timestamped before anyone acted on them. That is the
    property the ordering existed to protect, and it survives intact.

Scope, stated plainly: this document's rules are written for the plates allowlist
on Ink — the seed is an Ink block and the allocation is plates — while the
Robinhood intake has no plates collection and cannot have one. For those
registrants the hash pins the criteria text, not a drawing that runs on their
chain.

Ink Sepolia carries an earlier commitment that cannot be reproduced. Do not cite
it. Transaction

    0xc77c7788259d188297005b714f55d0f611a1adc16d0a08244d613bf8e0d1f93f

block 58669419 at 2026-08-25 15:45:15 UTC, put

    0x8d07eb4ed96b78f7fd03736e5c7aecd800cc94958f0028268b2172679e17677f

on chain 87 seconds before the waitlist 0x90a1620578CE419242F806e7387Db7e70c8cfa96
deployed at block 58669506 — so it honoured the ordering clause this publication
cannot. It fails the other half instead. That hash matches no version of
ALLOWLIST.md in this repository, under LF or CRLF: it was taken over a
working-tree draft, the document was first committed seven hours later at 1e14a00,
and 511aae0 then replaced the selection mechanism outright with qualified-referral
rank. Nobody can recompute 0x8d07eb4e…677f from the public repo, which is exactly
the reading web/lib/links.ts warns about — a reader hashing what they find and
getting 32 different bytes concludes the rules changed. So that transaction stays
out of the announcement. This file exists because of it; the commit that created
this file, 2680a91, is titled "Make the criteria hash reproducible before it goes
on chain."

Sepolia was never republished, and is not being republished now. Its window closed
2026-09-01 with a registration already in it, so a hash posted there today would
sit below neither the deploy nor that registration.
